// =====================================================================
// AP08 - Automation Account runbook -> RBAC escalation
//        (execution in the Azure MANAGEMENT PLANE via a runbook that runs
//         AS the over-privileged system-assigned Managed Identity of the
//         Automation Account)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
//   CHAIN (exploit):
//     1. AUTHORING: a principal with Automation Contributor over the RG creates/imports and
//        PUBLISHES a PowerShell runbook in the Automation Account.
//          runbooks/write + runbooks/draft/content/write + runbooks/publish/action  [T1651 precursor]
//        (in the lab this is done by the Terraform apply = the "loaded gun"; the defender
//         SEES the weapon being planted, parallel to 4899/4900 of AP05 and storageAccounts/write of AP07.)
//     2. EXECUTION: the same low-priv LAUNCHES a runbook job (Start-AzAutomationRunbook).
//          jobs/write                                                               [T1651 - Cloud Administration Command]
//        (Terraform NEVER launches the job: jobs/write only appears when the STUDENT triggers the "exploit".)
//     3. The job runs AS the MI (Connect-AzAccount -Identity). Since the MI holds User
//        Access Administrator or Owner OVER THE RG (both include
//        Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/write), the runbook executes
//        New-AzRoleAssignment and SELF-GRANTS Owner of the RG to the low-priv attacker.
//          roleAssignments/write with Caller == objectId of the MI                     [T1098.003 - GOLDEN SIGNAL]
//     4. PERSISTENCE: the low-priv is now Owner of the RG (full control + standing).  [T1078.004]
//
//   The effective ACTOR of the escalation is the Automation Account's MI (parity with AP02,
//   where the actor is the MI stolen via IMDS): the confused deputy is "whoever can LAUNCH
//   a runbook acts with the scope of the MI".
//
//   Sources (REAL tables in Log Analytics / Sentinel):
//     - AzureActivity    (MANAGEMENT plane; flows to the SIEM without provisioning ANYTHING -as in
//                         AP02/AP07-): runbook authoring, job launch
//                         (jobs/write = T1651) and the roleAssignments/write BY the MI.
//     - AzureDiagnostics (Automation Account DATA plane; ResourceProvider ==
//                         'MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION', Category in ('JobLogs','JobStreams').
//                         Automation has NO dedicated table -> the diagnostic setting WITHOUT
//                         log_analytics_destination_type lands in AzureDiagnostics, NOT in
//                         a Dedicated table like the 'StorageBlobLogs' of AP07).
//
//   MITRE:  T1651     (Cloud Administration Command)                 [CORE - execute via runbook]
//           T1098.003 (Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles) (the self-grant of Owner)
//           T1078.004 (Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts)               (persistence as Owner of the RG)
//
//   Sigma / KQL SPLIT (declared EXPLICITLY, like AP02 'the KV AuditEvent is not
//     activitylogs' and AP07 'StorageBlobLogs is not a Sigma logsource'):
//       * The MANAGEMENT PLANE (AzureActivity: authoring + jobs/write + roleAssignments/write)
//         has a companion Sigma rule (AP08-automation-runbook-rbac.yml).
//       * BUT the GOLDEN SIGNAL -roleAssignments/write with Caller == the MI- depends on an
//         objectId that VARIES per deployment: a static Sigma rule cannot fix it. That
//         narrowing (Caller==MI) is KQL-primary (parameter mi_principal_id, below).
//       * The DATA PLANE (JobLogs/JobStreams: the execution + the text New-AzRoleAssignment
//         in the streams) is NOT a standard Sigma logsource -> KQL-primary (THIS file).
//
//   CAVEATS of the schema/telemetry (like the KB5014754 block of AP05 / StorageBlobLogs of AP07):
//     * JobLogs/JobStreams are NOT active by default -> without the diagnostic setting on the
//       Automation Account, the runbook EXECUTION does NOT exist in ANY SIEM (exact mirror of
//       AP07 'without the blobServices/default diagnostic there are no logs' and of AP05 'without AuditFilter
//       there are no 4886/4887'). The MANAGEMENT plane (jobs/write, roleAssignments/write) DOES flow without
//       provisioning anything.
//     * deploy-vs-attack DISCRIMINATOR (the key to the GOLDEN SIGNAL): in the lab APPLY the grant
//       MI->role (azurerm_role_assignment) is executed by the DEPLOYER -> Caller == Terraform identity.
//       In the ATTACK the self-grant is executed by the MI -> Caller == objectId of the MI. Filtering Caller==MI
//       leaves out the deployment grant and isolates the runtime escalation.
//     * The BENEFICIARY of the roleAssignments/write (the objectId that receives Owner) is NOT serialized
//       reliably in AzureActivity (the request body does not travel in full) -> it is EXTRACTED as a tolerant
//       HINT from Properties and, with high fidelity, from the JobStreams (ResultDescription); it NEVER
//       gates the row (OR-not-AND, AP04/AP07 lesson: do not drop the chain).
//     * The Automation Account name carries a random suffix -> this KQL anchors on the FIXED RG
//       ('azrange-ap08-rg') and on the FIXED DECOY runbook ('azrange-ap08-maintenance'); fill
//       mi_principal_id with the output ap08_mi_principal_id to activate the golden filter.
//     * If your DCR/pipeline serializes the Automation fields (RunbookName_s, JobId_g,
//       StreamType_s, ResultDescription) differently, adjust against a real
//       AzureDiagnostics | where ResourceProvider == 'MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION' row.
//
//   Managed COMPLEMENT: Microsoft Defender for Cloud (anomalous role assignment) + Azure Policy
//     (deny Owner/UAA to automation identities) + PIM (no standing Owner/UAA). Use in parallel.
//
//   Author: Azure Attack Range   Date: 2026-11-15
// =====================================================================

let lookback         = 1d;
let corr_window      = 20m;                        // window job-launch -> MI-grant (OUTPUT 2)
let rg_name          = "azrange-ap08-rg";          // = ${lab_prefix}-ap08-rg (output ap08_resource_group); "" = any RG
let runbook_name     = "azrange-ap08-maintenance"; // = output ap08_runbook_name (fixed decoy); "" = any runbook
let mi_principal_id  = "";                          // = output ap08_mi_principal_id (objectId of the system-assigned MI).
                                                    //   FILL IN: it is the GOLDEN filter (Caller==MI). "" = does NOT filter (broader
                                                    //   triage over all roleAssignments/write of the RG; OR-not-AND).

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL A - T1651 (precursor), MANAGEMENT plane: runbook AUTHORING. Create/update
//   the runbook, write its draft content and PUBLISH it. In the lab it is triggered by the
//   Terraform apply (the loaded gun): the defender SEES the weapon being planted. Caller = the deployer (in
//   the apply) or the low-priv author (if authored by hand). On its own it is NOT an attack -> context.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalA_authoring =
    AzureActivity
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where OperationNameValue in~ (
          "MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION/AUTOMATIONACCOUNTS/RUNBOOKS/WRITE",
          "MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION/AUTOMATIONACCOUNTS/RUNBOOKS/DRAFT/CONTENT/WRITE",
          "MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION/AUTOMATIONACCOUNTS/RUNBOOKS/PUBLISH/ACTION")
    | where rg_name == "" or ResourceGroup =~ rg_name
    | where ActivityStatusValue in~ ("Success", "Accept", "Start")
    | extend Stage = case(
          OperationNameValue has "PUBLISH",        "T1651 (precursor) - runbook PUBLISHED (draft -> published; the loaded gun)",
          OperationNameValue has "DRAFT/CONTENT",  "T1651 (precursor) - runbook content written (payload authoring)",
                                                   "T1651 (precursor) - runbook created/updated")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "A-authoring",
              Stage,
              Plane    = "mgmt",
              OperationName = OperationNameValue,
              Caller,                         // deployer (apply) or low-priv author
              CallerIp = CallerIpAddress,
              ResourceGroup,
              Resource = _ResourceId,
              Status   = ActivityStatusValue;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL B - T1651 (core), MANAGEMENT plane: EXECUTION. Launch of a runbook job
//   (jobs/write). Terraform NEVER triggers it -> jobs/write appears ONLY when the STUDENT
//   runs the "exploit" (Start-AzAutomationRunbook). The JobId is extracted from the _ResourceId so
//   it can be joined with the JobStreams (data-plane) in OUTPUT 2. LauncherIsMI is ANNOTATED
//   (does not filter): in the attack the launcher is the low-priv, not the MI.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalB_jobexec =
    AzureActivity
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where OperationNameValue =~ "MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION/AUTOMATIONACCOUNTS/JOBS/WRITE"
    | where rg_name == "" or ResourceGroup =~ rg_name
    | where ActivityStatusValue in~ ("Success", "Accept", "Start")
    | extend JobId = tolower(extract(@'(?i)/jobs/([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12})', 1, tostring(_ResourceId)))
    | extend LauncherIsMI = mi_principal_id != "" and Caller =~ mi_principal_id
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "B-job-exec",
              Stage    = "T1651 - runbook job launched (execution = the student's imperative exploit)",
              Plane    = "mgmt",
              OperationName = OperationNameValue,
              Caller,                         // the low-priv driving the MI
              CallerIp = CallerIpAddress,
              ResourceGroup,
              Resource = _ResourceId,
              JobId,
              LauncherIsMI,
              Status   = ActivityStatusValue;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL C - T1098.003 (GOLDEN SIGNAL), MANAGEMENT plane: roleAssignments/write whose Caller IS
//   the Automation Account's MI. A role assignment executed BY an automation identity
//   is extremely high signal (no automation should hand out RBAC). If mi_principal_id is set
//   it filters to Caller==MI (high fidelity and leaves out the DEPLOYMENT grant, whose Caller is the
//   deployer). If empty the row is NOT discarded: ALL roleAssignments/write of the
//   RG are emitted with GrantByAutomationMI as an annotation so the analyst can triage (OR-not-AND, AP04/AP07).
//   The BENEFICIARY (objectId that receives Owner) is attempted to be extracted from Properties as a HINT; it does
//   not gate (the request body does not travel reliably -> it is confirmed via JobStreams in OUTPUT 2).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalC_mi_grant =
    AzureActivity
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where OperationNameValue =~ "MICROSOFT.AUTHORIZATION/ROLEASSIGNMENTS/WRITE"
    | where rg_name == "" or ResourceGroup =~ rg_name
    | where ActivityStatusValue in~ ("Success", "Accept", "Start")
    | where mi_principal_id == "" or Caller =~ mi_principal_id
    | extend GrantByAutomationMI = mi_principal_id != "" and Caller =~ mi_principal_id
    | extend BeneficiaryHint = tolower(extract(@'(?i)principalid"?\s*[:=]\s*"?([0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12})', 1, tostring(Properties)))
    | extend Stage = iff(GrantByAutomationMI,
          "T1098.003 - roleAssignments/write BY the Automation MI (golden signal: self-granted RBAC escalation)",
          "T1098.003 - roleAssignments/write in the AP08 RG (triage: confirm whether the Caller is the Automation MI)")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "C-mi-roleassign",
              Stage,
              Plane    = "mgmt",
              OperationName = OperationNameValue,
              Caller,                         // objectId of the MI (gold) or the granting principal
              CallerIp = CallerIpAddress,
              ResourceGroup,
              Resource = _ResourceId,
              GrantByAutomationMI,
              BeneficiaryHint,
              Status   = ActivityStatusValue;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL D - T1651 / T1098.003, DATA plane (AzureDiagnostics, Automation). JobLogs =
//   job state changes; JobStreams = the output streams. With log_verbose=true and the
//   output NOT suppressed, ResultDescription reveals the literal New-AzRoleAssignment / 'Owner' of the
//   "exploit" (OPPORTUNISTIC data-plane; a stealthy attacker would suppress it with | Out-Null -> that is why
//   the GOLDEN leg lives in the UNSUPPRESSIBLE control-plane of SignalC). The _s/_g fields of Automation
//   are read with column_ifexists so the query is portable to workspaces without Automation logs.
//   REMEMBER: WITHOUT the Automation Account's diagnostic setting this table is EMPTY for AP08.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
let SignalD_jobdata =
    AzureDiagnostics
    | where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
    | where ResourceProvider == "MICROSOFT.AUTOMATION"
    | where Category in ("JobLogs", "JobStreams")
    | extend RunbookName = tostring(column_ifexists("RunbookName_s", ""))
    | extend JobId       = tolower(tostring(column_ifexists("JobId_g", "")))
    | extend StreamType  = tostring(column_ifexists("StreamType_s", ""))
    | where runbook_name == "" or RunbookName =~ runbook_name
    | where rg_name == "" or _ResourceId has rg_name
    | extend RoleAssignmentTextHit = Category == "JobStreams"
             and ResultDescription has_any ("New-AzRoleAssignment", "roleAssignment", "RoleDefinitionName", "Owner")
    | extend Stage = case(
          RoleAssignmentTextHit,     "T1651/T1098.003 - job stream reveals role assignment text (New-AzRoleAssignment/Owner)",
          Category == "JobStreams",  "T1651 - runbook job output stream (data-plane)",
                                     "T1651 - runbook job state change (JobLogs)")
    | project TimeGenerated,
              Signal   = "D-job-dataplane",
              Stage,
              Plane    = "data",
              OperationName = Category,
              ResourceGroup = toupper(tostring(split(tostring(_ResourceId), "/")[4])),  // toupper: aligns with AzureActivity.ResourceGroup (uppercase) in the union timeline
              Resource = _ResourceId,
              RunbookName,
              JobId,
              StreamType,
              JobStatus = ResultType,
              RoleAssignmentTextHit,
              ResultDescription;

// =====================================================================
// OUTPUT 1 - Unified timeline of the 4 AP08 signals (independent; union = OR).
// Triage of the full chain (exploit):
//   SIGNAL A (authoring + PUBLICATION of the runbook = the gun loaded by the apply)  ->  SIGNAL B
//   (jobs/write = the student LAUNCHES the job, T1651)  ->  SIGNAL C (roleAssignments/write BY the MI
//   = the self-grant of Owner, the golden signal)  ->  SIGNAL D (JobStreams reveals the text
//   New-AzRoleAssignment, if the diagnostic is active). Each signal fires ON ITS OWN (isfuzzy
//   supports the heterogeneous mgmt/data schemas and the absent tables; NEVER a global AND that
//   discards a branch when a plane is missing -AP04/AP07 lesson-).
// =====================================================================
union isfuzzy=true SignalA_authoring, SignalB_jobexec, SignalC_mi_grant, SignalD_jobdata
| sort by TimeGenerated asc


// =====================================================================
// OUTPUT 2 (high fidelity) - Correlate the CHAIN: job-launch (low-priv) -> MI-grant (the MI).
// The CORE is an INNER join of TWO control-plane events that ALWAYS flow to AzureActivity and
// that are BOTH indispensable in the chain:
//   (a) jobs/write whose Caller is NOT the MI (the low-priv that launches the runbook)       [T1651]
//   (b) roleAssignments/write whose Caller IS the MI, in the SAME RG, within corr_window        [T1098.003]
//       after (a).
// Near-zero FP: it is exactly the pivot that remediation (removing UAA/Owner from the MI) makes impossible.
// The inner join between (a) and (b) is CORRECT -it is NOT the AP07 bug- because both links are
// MANDATORY and both management events flow without provisioning anything. What is OPTIONAL (the beneficiary
// via JobStreams, which requires the diagnostic setting OFF by default) goes with LEFTOUTER and is ANNOTATED,
// NEVER gates: if the data-plane is off the chain STILL fires by RG+time (AP04/AP07 lesson:
// do not drop the chain). The fan-out of the leftouter is collapsed with summarize. The correlation
// is by RG+TIME, NOT by the beneficiary (which does not serialize reliably in AzureActivity); the beneficiary
// is only ANNOTATED, and BeneficiaryIsLauncher=true (the low-priv that launched the job IS who receives Owner) is
// the smoking gun. Uncomment to alert.
// =====================================================================
